[0.174128, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1mtoolInterfacer\u001b[0m\u001b[2m  ·  one intent in, one answer out, plus the receipt\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n  service   http://127.0.0.1:44779   (9 ops registered)\r\n  deciding  \u001b[36mfixture\u001b[0m  \u001b[2m(recorded answers — deterministic, offline)\u001b[0m\r\n  tools     \u001b[2mthe repo fixtures (tests/data/fake_cli.py) — deterministic\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  files     /tmp/ti-demo-files-5krlfugp\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  note: scene 3's picks are recorded answers, not a model's. Run with\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m        --live to see the configured backend actually decide.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[1.174991, "o", "\u001b[1mscene 1 — the caller names the operation\u001b[0m\r\n  intent  \u001b[36m'read notes.md'\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m          L0 passthrough — no decision is made, so there is nothing to reason about\u001b[0m\r\n"]
